WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.122 --> 00:00:01.932
(mischievous music)

00:00:01.932 --> 00:00:03.136
- [Narrator] New York City,

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:06.040
the bagel capital of the world.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.013
The place where bagels reign supreme,

00:00:08.013 --> 00:00:09.668
and are a cut above the rest.

00:00:09.668 --> 00:00:10.983
Right?

00:00:10.983 --> 00:00:12.531
Well, maybe not.

00:00:12.531 --> 00:00:13.412
Because it turns out,

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:15.086
there's something that could rock New York

00:00:15.086 --> 00:00:16.333
and its precious bagels

00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:17.828
to the core.

00:00:17.828 --> 00:00:20.828
(mischievous music)

00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:26.696
Montreal has their own
booming bagel industry,

00:00:26.696 --> 00:00:28.996
and there's a constituency
of bagel enthusiasts

00:00:28.996 --> 00:00:31.129
that actually consider Montreal bagels

00:00:31.129 --> 00:00:32.554
better than New York's.

00:00:32.554 --> 00:00:33.387
Shocking,

00:00:33.387 --> 00:00:34.220
I know.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.952
- [Woman] I lived in
New York for 50 years,

00:00:35.952 --> 00:00:37.964
but I don't care for the New York bagels.

00:00:37.964 --> 00:00:40.214
And neither does my family.

00:00:44.428 --> 00:00:45.843
- [Narrator] What is going on here?

00:00:45.843 --> 00:00:46.734
It's time to investigate.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:47.924
- My name is Robert Morena,

00:00:47.924 --> 00:00:50.228
and I'm the co-owner of
St-Viateur Bagel Shop.

00:00:50.228 --> 00:00:51.130
People really know about us,

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.969
and they know that if
you come to Montreal,

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:54.673
you've gotta try a Montreal bagel.

00:00:54.673 --> 00:00:56.308
Every time I go to New York,

00:00:56.308 --> 00:00:59.137
I always visit a bagel bakery.

00:00:59.137 --> 00:01:01.054
And I test my bagels against theirs;

00:01:01.054 --> 00:01:03.543
and I've yet to come across something

00:01:03.543 --> 00:01:06.793
that compares to a St-Viateur bagel.

00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:09.774
(mischievous music)

00:01:09.774 --> 00:01:11.252
A Montreal bagel

00:01:11.252 --> 00:01:13.020
is set aside by its process

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.513
of how it's made.

00:01:14.513 --> 00:01:16.834
We hand-roll each bagel.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.102
We boil it in honey water.

00:01:18.102 --> 00:01:19.677
We seed it.

00:01:19.677 --> 00:01:21.304
We bake it in a wood-fired oven.

00:01:21.304 --> 00:01:22.137
- [Narrator] Alright,

00:01:22.137 --> 00:01:24.190
so Montreal's got the
sweet and doughy flavor.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:25.277
What do you got to say about that,

00:01:25.277 --> 00:01:26.110
New York?

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.054
- Montreal bagels?

00:01:27.054 --> 00:01:27.887
Eh.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:28.761
I think it's mostly a fad.

00:01:28.761 --> 00:01:29.594
Honey water?

00:01:29.594 --> 00:01:30.427
Who does that?

00:01:30.427 --> 00:01:31.260
No, I'm kidding.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.093
I'm just making that up.

00:01:32.093 --> 00:01:32.926
Sorry.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.759
My name is Darin Dolfi,

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:34.592
and I'm the operations manager

00:01:34.592 --> 00:01:35.890
with H&amp;H Midtown Bagels East.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:36.723
If you want a regular bagel,

00:01:36.723 --> 00:01:37.616
you can go anywhere.

00:01:37.616 --> 00:01:39.055
If you want a true New York City staple,

00:01:39.055 --> 00:01:41.538
you come to H&amp;H Midtown Bagels East.

00:01:41.538 --> 00:01:42.371
Look,

00:01:42.371 --> 00:01:43.204
it's New York City.

00:01:43.204 --> 00:01:44.144
We're moving at a fast pace.

00:01:44.144 --> 00:01:45.267
We sell a lot of bagels.

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:46.915
Some bagels are made on a machine,

00:01:46.915 --> 00:01:47.748
others are hand-rolled,

00:01:47.748 --> 00:01:49.231
like our cinnamon raisin.

00:01:49.231 --> 00:01:50.064
Big deal,

00:01:50.064 --> 00:01:50.897
still same great taste.

00:01:50.897 --> 00:01:52.759
It's a very labor-intensive process …

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:54.949
That takes roughly 24 hours
from start to finish

00:01:54.949 --> 00:01:56.972
before we can bake off the bagels.

00:01:56.972 --> 00:01:58.989
- [Narrator] So you each
have your own process.

00:01:58.989 --> 00:01:59.915
Big deal.

00:01:59.915 --> 00:02:01.192
How do you eat them?

00:02:01.192 --> 00:02:02.025
- So, generally,

00:02:02.025 --> 00:02:03.154
we do not cut our bagels.

00:02:03.154 --> 00:02:04.903
And they come out of a wood-fired oven,

00:02:04.903 --> 00:02:06.281
they don't need to be toasted.

00:02:06.281 --> 00:02:07.114
You come,

00:02:07.114 --> 00:02:07.947
you pick up the bagels,

00:02:07.947 --> 00:02:09.557
and they buy a tub of cream cheese,

00:02:09.557 --> 00:02:11.950
and you would make the bagels yourself.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:15.012
That's the real Montreal
way of doing things.

00:02:15.012 --> 00:02:15.845
- [Narrator] Got it.

00:02:15.845 --> 00:02:16.678
So in Montreal,

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:17.730
I have to make it myself.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.879
What about in New York?

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:21.257
- [Darin] When you walk in
to H&amp;H Midtown Bagels East,

00:02:21.257 --> 00:02:22.159
you walk up to the counter,

00:02:22.159 --> 00:02:22.992
place your order,

00:02:22.992 --> 00:02:23.825
we slice the bagel,

00:02:23.825 --> 00:02:24.658
we put cream cheese,

00:02:24.658 --> 00:02:25.491
we put the lox,

00:02:25.491 --> 00:02:26.324
we wrap it up,

00:02:26.324 --> 00:02:27.371
and it's ready to go.

00:02:27.371 --> 00:02:29.374
- [Robert] New York started
manufacturing bagels

00:02:29.374 --> 00:02:30.731
before Montreal.

00:02:30.731 --> 00:02:32.090
The big difference is that

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.873
we just kept our bagel-making
tradition the same.

00:02:35.873 --> 00:02:37.294
Still horse and wagon.

00:02:37.294 --> 00:02:38.915
- [Narrator] So if you're
more of a sweet and doughy,

00:02:38.915 --> 00:02:40.391
do-it-yourself bagel maker,

00:02:40.391 --> 00:02:41.958
Montreal's for you.

00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:43.410
But if you prefer the toasted bagel

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.875
with everything on it,

00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:46.093
you gotta come to New York.

00:02:46.093 --> 00:02:47.201
But in the end,

00:02:47.201 --> 00:02:49.965
if there's one thing we can all agree on,

00:02:49.965 --> 00:02:50.930
it's that everything's better

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.438
with cream cheese.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.438
(mischievous music)

00:02:58.839 --> 00:03:00.756
(bing)

